        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-02T11:21:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The HAL should wrap any access to the ref DT, which we\u0027ll keep only as a fallback (to be deprecated) to the \"actual\" call, when implementing v2. So, yes, combined with VBMeta parsing for the guest `/vendor` pubkey/hash it should remove the need for the ref DST in the client code (`virtmgr`). Cc: @ioffe@google.com\n\nIdeally, we\u0027d also want to make it harder for HAL implementations to rely on the DT instead of implementing the call, to discourage new implementations from shipping the deprecated API (no idea how this could be done).",
      "parentUuid": "7c1826f8_daabb571",
      "revId": "8082ff5611885fac7c278a988e96358623da9fab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
