      "writtenOn": "2024-12-02T11:21:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, for the explanation, I had misunderstood `SecretkeeperProxy` as being the entity that talks to Sk from the host.\n\n\u003e What\u0027s the right \"unimplemented\" here?\n\nLet\u0027s not panic (`unimplemented!()`) from a library. I don\u0027t know where those error codes are documented but, from the variant names alone, `ExceptionCode::SECURITY`, `ExceptionCode::ILLEGAL_STATE` or even `ExceptionCode::SERVICE_SPECIFIC` might be better candidates, given that the option _is_ actually supported (or should be) but we don\u0027t want it to be used.",
      "parentUuid": "6ce01989_60f42570",
